From d2baa7bdc3558015f8122b587d6f8fc313bd31ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:57:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: after a refresh of the modes, the choices of a
 start

The refresh of the mode list kept each resolution by the timing of its mode
where the display still offered it, the desktop resolution among them. With
HDMI Deep Colour turned on while Kodi runs, the interface stayed in the
desktop mode of the HDMI 1.4 list (2160p30), where a restart gives 2160p60.

Now every choice is the one a start makes with the new list:
- the desktop resolution is the mode that the display prefers
  (MODELIST::PreferredPlace(), which is CDRMUtils::FindPreferredMode(): what a
  start takes where the console left no mode; the console takes that one),
  matched to its resolution as UpdateResolutions() matches it at a start;
- the current resolution is CDisplaySettings::GetDisplayResolution(), with the
  fallback of CApplication::CreateGUI(): "desktop" in the settings names the
  new desktop resolution; a resolution of the settings that is still offered
  is kept; one that is not falls back to the nearest;
- the interface is set in it. Where the mode on the screen is already that one
  (MODELIST::ScreenStays(), by its timing), no mode is set: its resolution only
  takes its new place (ApplyModeChange()).
A list with the same modes in the same places and the same one preferred is
the same list (a start makes the same choices with it); before, another
preferred mode did not count.

#39956 says what the interface uses now ("The display now offers other modes.
The interface now uses {0}."): it can change also where its mode is still
offered.

Host test: what a refresh leaves is compared with what a start on the new list
gives (the resolutions, the desktop one, the current one, the interface's, the
mode on the screen, and whether a mode was set): the C5 going from HDMI 1.4 to
Deep Colour and back with the settings at desktop, 1080p60, 2160p60 (gone, and
offered again), 2160p30 and 1080i60, the interface left in the mode of a video,
a monitor and the TV, another preferred mode; and 20000 random lists. It fails
with the rule before (21 checks of the cases, 12355 random lists), with the
list of the start kept (47 and 17088) and with a refresh by index (33 and
16222). 19 mutations of the header caught. Nothing of this has run on a
graphics card.
